                        "glosses": [
                            "To sow (seed) where something has already been sown."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "adbc51fc-48ab-40af-8cbd-676b42aaed3e",
                                "sense_id": "921bc333-c255-3713-b1f5-55f8132b6f9a",
                                "text": "The which contrary corrupt seede of false doctrine we right well know came of the sayd aduersary, because it was long after ouersowen[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb45c042-c249-40fd-b25d-abe5d8bbe66f",
                                "sense_id": "921bc333-c255-3713-b1f5-55f8132b6f9a",
                                "text": "But vvhen men vvere a ſleepe, his enemy came and ouerſovved cockle among the vvheate, and vvent his vvay."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8e487c6-fd75-4f37-9918-a8d14454d6cd",
                                "sense_id": "921bc333-c255-3713-b1f5-55f8132b6f9a",
                                "text": "[…] it is possible to oversow the area with improved forages. […] Vigorous species must be used to oversow the area […]"
                            }
                        ]
